        \"C) take over\",\n        \"D) cut through\"\n      ]\n      ,\n      \"answer\": \"D\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 26,\n      \"question\": \"Which dependent preposition is used in 'There are many books on the table'?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) of\",\n        \"B) with\",\n        \"C) at\",\n        \"D) on\"\n      ]\n      ,\n      \"answer\": \"D\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 27,\n      \"question\": \"Which precise lexical choice is correct?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) 'It's been a while since I saw you last.'\",\n        \"B) 'She hasn't changed much over the years.'\",\n        \"C) 'He was very difficult to understand what he said.'\",\n        \"D) 'They are quite affluent for their young age.'\"\n      ]\n      ,\n      \"answer\": \"C\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 28,\n      \"question\": \"Which of the following is a correct use of 'even though'?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) Even though it was raining, we went for a walk.\",\n        \"B) Despite the fact that he didn't like pizza, he ate three slices.\",\n        \"C) Although she had no experience, she was hired for the job.\",\n        \"D) She studied hard even though her parents didn't care.\"\n      ]\n      ,\n      \"answer\": \"A\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 29,\n      \"question\": \"Which reported speech is correct?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) She said that she would come.\",\n        \"B) He told me he had finished the project.\",\n        \"C) They suggested we should go.\",\n        \"D) We were informed that there was an emergency.\"\n      ]\n      ,\n      \"answer\": \"B\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 30,\n      \"question\": \"Which dependent clause is correct?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) When I finish my work.\",\n        \"B) Because she was tired.\",\n        \"C) As soon as the meeting ended.\",\n        \"D) In spite of her illness.\"\n      ]